        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style=\"container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%\"><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;height:100%;background:#e9f0ff;color:#121a33;font-family:system-ui;padding:3.4cqw 4cqw;border-top:1.2cqw solid #2254b6;overflow:auto\"><div style=\"font:800 2.6cqw/1.2 system-ui;color:#2254b6;letter-spacing:.14em\">PROJECT / START HERE</div><div style=\"font:850 6.3cqw/1.04 system-ui;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:1.3cqw 0 1.7cqw\">Make it your own.</div><div style=\"font:500 3.2cqw/1.35 system-ui;margin-bottom:2cqw\">A project says why it exists, how it is going, and keeps everything gathered around it.</div><div style=\"display:grid;gap:1.2cqw;font:500 2.8cqw/1.3 system-ui\"><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #a9c9ff;padding-top:1.1cqw\"><b style=\"color:#2254b6\">01 / HOME</b> · Name the project, set its purpose and current standing.</div><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #a9c9ff;padding-top:1.1cqw\"><b style=\"color:#2254b6\">02 / SHELVES</b> · Ideas, Plans, Tasks, Decisions and Notes are collections. Each has its own root graph.</div><div style=\"border-top:1px solid #a9c9ff;padding-top:1.1cqw\"><b style=\"color:#2254b6\">03 / WORK</b> · Make a graph from the appropriate template and connect it to its shelf with a portal.</div></div><div style=\"margin-top:2cqw;font:500 2.5cqw/1.3 system-ui;color:#41567e\">The shared Method derives the project views automatically. Import the Project template once for its class and Method.</div></div></div>"
        },
